    ("What does 'PBG' stand for in contract management?", "Performance Bank Guarantee (or e-PBG)", ["Public Bidding Guideline", "Procurement Balance Grant", "Pre-Bid Guarantee"], "A PBG is furnished by the successful winning bidder to secure satisfactory performance and fulfillment of contract obligations."),
    ("What is the typical percentage range of contract value required as Performance Security (PBG) under standard GFR rules?", "3% to 5% of the total value of the contract", ["20% to 25% of contract value", "50% of contract value", "100% of contract value"], "Normally set between 5% and 10%, it was temporarily rationalized to 3%-5% to support vendor working capital liquidity."),
    ("Under the Public Procurement Policy for MSEs Order, 2012, what mandatory annual procurement quota is reserved for Micro and Small Enterprises?", "At least 25% of total annual purchases of goods and services by Central Ministries, Departments, and CPSEs", ["At least 10% of total annual purchases", "At least 50% of total annual purchases", "At least 5% of total annual purchases"], "Central government bodies must source at least 25% of their total annual commercial procurement from eligible MSEs."),
