    ("Under GFR 2017, what is a 'Limited Tender Enquiry' (LTE)?", "A procurement method where tender invitations are sent directly to a pre-qualified list of registered suppliers", ["A tender published exclusively in foreign newspapers", "A secret bidding process conducted behind closed doors", "A verbal telephone quotation obtained from two local shops"], "LTE is adopted for purchases up to Rs 25 lakh or urgent requirements where open competitive advertisement is inefficient."),
    ("What is an 'Advertised (Open) Tender Enquiry' under GFR 2017?", "A public tender invitation open to all eligible bidders published on the Central Public Procurement Portal (CPPP) and GeM", ["A tender restricted strictly to government public sector undertakings", "An informal quotation sought via WhatsApp messaging", "A tender advertised only on local television channels"], "Open tender ensures universal public notice, robust competition, and transparency for procurements above the LTE threshold."),
    ("What is a 'Two-Bid System' (Two-Envelope System) in public tender evaluation?", "Bidders submit Technical Bids and Financial Bids separately; financial bids are opened only for technically qualified bidders", ["Bidders must submit two identical copies of their price quote", "Bidders must submit separate quotes for morning and evening work", "Bidders are given two chances to re-enter their price"], "The two-bid system prevents commercial price bias during technical evaluation, ensuring compliance before prices are revealed."),
    ("What is the primary role of a 'Pre-Bid Conference' in large public tenders?", "Clarifying tender specifications, addressing prospective bidder queries, and issuing formal amendments", ["Announcing the winning contractor before bids are opened", "Negotiating secret financial discounts with favored vendors", "Conducting police background checks on bidder executives"], "Pre-bid conferences ensure technical clarity, level the playing field, and prevent post-tender disputes and bid rejections."),
    ("What does 'Force Majeure' signify in public procurement contracts?", "Unforeseeable, unavoidable catastrophic events beyond human control (e.g., war, floods, pandemics) excusing contractual delay", ["The absolute authority of the buyer to terminate contracts at will", "The legal right of the supplier to double contract prices", "A military takeover of private industrial factories"], "Force Majeure relieves parties from contractual liability or liquidated damages when extraordinary events prevent performance."),
    ("What is a 'Rate Contract' in public procurement?", "An agreement with a supplier to furnish specified goods at fixed agreed rates over a designated time period", ["A contract that charges variable daily fluctuating prices", "A shipping agreement for marine cargo container freight", "A foreign currency hedging contract signed with the central bank"], "Rate contracts eliminate repetitive tendering for recurring common-use items, locking in bulk-discounted prices."),
    ("What does 'Golden Parameters' mean in GeM product catalog filtering?", "The most critical core technical specifications that define the primary functionality and classification of a product", ["The decorative aesthetic colors available for office furniture", "The luxury gold packaging required for executive deliveries", "The maximum retail profit margin allowed to the seller"], "Golden parameters allow automated, unbiased parametric filtering so buyers find functionally identical products across brands."),
    ("What does 'CPPP' stand for in Indian public e-procurement?", "Central Public Procurement Portal", ["Centralized Purchasing Program Plan", "Core Private Procurement Platform", "Commercial Public Partnership Portal"], "CPPP (eprocure.gov.in) is the national portal mandated by the Department of Expenditure for publishing all central e-tenders.")
