gem_med = [
    ("Under the 'Make in India' Public Procurement Order, what qualifies a bidder as a 'Class-I Local Supplier'?", "Goods or services offered have local domestic value addition equal to or exceeding 50%", ["Local domestic value addition between 20% and 50%", "Goods manufactured 100% in foreign overseas facilities", "Suppliers owned by local state municipal governments"], "Class-I local suppliers receive highest purchase preference in public tenders to promote domestic manufacturing."),
    ("Under GFR Rule 155, what is the purchase limit for procurement of goods by a Local Purchase Committee?", "Above Rs 25,000 and up to Rs 2,50,000 on each occasion based on joint market survey certificate", ["Above Rs 1,00,000 up to Rs 10,00,000", "Up to Rs 10,000 only", "Above Rs 5,00,000 up to Rs 25,00,000"], "Rule 155 authorizes a three-member Local Purchase Committee to certify reasonable quality and market price for purchases up to Rs 2.5 lakh."),
    ("Under the 'Make in India' Public Procurement Order, what qualifies a bidder as a 'Class-II Local Supplier'?", "Local domestic value addition is more than 20% but less than 50%", ["Local domestic value addition is greater than 50%", "Local domestic value addition is less than 10%", "The supplier has zero local manufacturing in India"], "Class-II suppliers are eligible to participate in domestic tenders but do not get purchase preference over Class-I suppliers."),
    ("Under the 'Make in India' Public Procurement Order, what is a 'Non-Local Supplier'?", "A supplier whose goods or services possess local value addition of 20% or less", ["A supplier whose headquarters is in another Indian state", "A supplier who does not possess a PAN card", "A vendor who fails to submit a bid security deposit"], "Non-local suppliers cannot participate in tenders reserved for local suppliers and are excluded from domestic preference margins."),
    ("What is the threshold limit up to which Global Tender Enquiries (GTE) are prohibited under GFR Rule 161(iv)?", "No Global Tender Enquiry can be issued for procurements up to Rs 200 crore without prior Cabinet Secretariat approval", ["Up to Rs 50 crore", "Up to Rs 500 crore", "Up to Rs 10 crore"], "To protect domestic industry and MSMEs from foreign dumping, global tenders below Rs 200 crore are banned in public procurement."),
    ("Under the MSE Purchase Preference policy, what is the 'L1 + 15%' purchase preference price band mechanism?", "MSEs quoting within L1+15% can match L1's price to supply at least 25% of the total tendered procurement quantity", ["MSEs quoting within 15% are automatically awarded 100% of the contract", "MSEs are granted a 15% cash cash subsidy from the central treasury", "MSEs can charge 15% higher prices without matching L1 rates"], "If L-1 is a non-MSE, participating MSEs within the 15% margin are invited to match L-1 price to secure 25% of the contract."),
    ("Under the Make in India policy, what is the 'Margin of Purchase Preference' granted to Class-I local suppliers?", "20% (if the lowest price L1 is Class-II or Non-Local, Class-I within L1+20% can match L1)", ["10%", "5%", "50%"], "The 20% margin allows domestic value-adding manufacturers to match the lowest quote and claim contract award."),
    ("What is 'Cartelization' or 'Bid Rigging' in public procurement, and which authority investigates it in India?", "Illegal collusion between competing bidders to manipulate tender prices, investigated by Competition Commission of India (CCI)", ["Legal joint ventures between state public sector companies", "Price discounts offered for prompt online payments", "A labor union negotiation conducted under the Factories Act"], "Cartelization eliminates genuine price discovery; Section 3 of the Competition Act, 2002 strictly prohibits anti-competitive bid rigging."),
    ("What is the 'Fall Clause' in government supply contracts?", "If the contractor sells the same product to any other customer at a lower price, the government contract price drops automatically", ["A safety penalty imposed if a factory worker falls from scaffolding", "A clause cancelling the contract if autumn winter weather arrives", "A clause allowing the government to delay payments during revenue drops"], "The Fall Clause ensures the government always enjoys the lowest price available in the open commercial market."),
    ("What is 'Single Tender Enquiry' (Proprietary Tender) under GFR Rule 166?", "Procuring goods from a single source when only one specific firm is known to manufacture the required item", ["A tender where only one single printed application form is sold", "A tender that allows only bachelor individuals to submit bids", "A tender that expires within 24 hours of public announcement"], "Procurement from a single firm without competition is strictly regulated and requires PAC certification and administrative justification."),
    ("What is 'Push-Button Procurement' on the GeM portal?", "An automated algorithmic workflow enabling instant bulk order placement against dynamic lowest rates", ["A physical panic button installed in government procurement offices", "An emergency tender issued for disaster management supplies", "A system where suppliers push products directly to office doors"], "Push-button procurement streamlines high-volume, standard repetitive departmental orders with zero human intervention delays."),
    ("What does 'Custom Bid' enable buyers to do on the GeM portal?", "Procure complex, customized products or services whose exact specifications are not available in standard GeM catalogs", ["Order custom tailor-made formal uniforms for senior executives", "Bypass all GFR rules and award contracts without competition", "Purchase foreign luxury automobiles directly from overseas"], "Custom bidding allows creation of bespoke technical parameters while retaining GeM's transparent digital bidding framework."),
    ("What is the primary function of the 'Incident Management Policy' on the GeM portal?", "Investigating and penalizing buyer and seller deviations, defaults, fake documents, and delivery failures", ["Managing accidental workplace fires and physical computer crashes", "Handling public road traffic accidents during product deliveries", "Providing medical first-aid training to warehouse logistics workers"], "Incident management investigates violations and issues warning notifications, red flags, catalog suspensions, or permanent debarment."),
    ("Under GeM's incident management system, what is an 'Orange Flag' or 'Red Flag' on a seller's profile?", "A public system penalty flag warning buyers of repeated delivery defaults or contractual non-compliance", ["An award badge honoring outstanding product manufacturing quality", "A notification that the seller operates in a border district", "A badge indicating the seller accepts cash-on-delivery payments"], "Flags impact seller reputation and can lead to automatic disqualification from future bidding cycles."),
    ("What does 'Debarment' (Blacklisting) under GFR Rule 151 entail?", "Excluding a corrupt, fraudulent, or defaulting bidder from participating in any government procurement for up to 3 years", ["Restricting an executive from visiting government departmental offices", "Cancelling a company's commercial corporate banking license", "A fine equal to 100% of corporate executive annual salaries"], "GFR 151 mandates debarment for offenses under the Prevention of Corruption Act or severe breaches of procurement integrity."),
    ("What is the maximum period of Debarment for conviction under the Prevention of Corruption Act or IPC?", "Up to 3 years from the date of debarment order", ["Permanent lifetime ban from all human economic activities", "Exactly 6 months", "Up to 10 years unconditionally"], "Debarment under GFR Rule 151(i) for criminal corruption or breach of integrity cannot exceed 3 years across all ministries."),
    ("What is 'Integrity Pact' (IP) in large-scale public procurement?", "A binding commitment between buyer and bidders committing both sides to refrain from bribery, collusion, and corruption", ["An agreement between competing companies to fix retail prices", "An employment bond signed between managers and staff", "A treaty signed between sovereign states to lower import tariffs"], "Monitored by Independent External Monitors (IEMs), IPs are mandated for high-value tenders (typically above Rs 5-10 crore)."),
    ("Who acts as an 'Independent External Monitor' (IEM) under an Integrity Pact?", "Eminent persons of high integrity (retired judges, civil servants, or PSUs chiefs) who independently review complaints", ["Active sitting executives of the competing bidding corporations", "Junior clerks working in the procurement tender cell", "Commercial credit agency debt collection officers"], "IEMs independently investigate vendor grievances regarding tender irregularities, bias, or integrity violations."),
    ("What is the 'Option Clause' in public procurement contracts?", "The buyer's right to increase or decrease the ordered quantity by up to 25% to 30% at contracted unit prices during delivery", ["The seller's option to cancel the order if market costs increase", "The vendor's right to deliver alternative non-compliant brands", "The buyer's option to pay half the price if budget is cut"], "The Option Clause accommodates operational demand variations without requiring fresh lengthy tendering cycles."),
    ("What is 'Price Variation Clause' (PVC) in long-term procurement contracts?", "A formula allowing contract prices to adjust transparently in response to audited shifts in raw material or labor indices", ["An arbitrary surcharge added by the contractor at final delivery", "A discount given to customers who pay within 24 hours", "A tariff adjustment imposed by the World Trade Organization"], "PVC protects both parties against catastrophic commodity swings in contracts extending over long execution horizons."),
    ("Under GFR Rule 170, when can 'Bid Security Declaration' be accepted in lieu of cash Earnest Money Deposit (EMD)?", "When authorized by the Ministry of Finance, allowing bidders to sign a declaration accepting debarment if they withdraw bids", ["Only when a bidder is personal friends with the procurement director", "Whenever the total contract value exceeds Rs 1,000 crore", "Only for foreign multinational aerospace corporations"], "Bid Security Declarations were widely deployed to boost bidder participation during post-pandemic liquidity distress."),
    ("In GeM, what is the role of the 'Primary User' (HOD / Organization Head)?", "Creating secondary user accounts (Buyers, Consignees, and PAOs) and overseeing organizational procurement operations", ["Bidding on tenders to sell surplus office paper to other ministries", "Auditing the national treasury annual tax revenue", "Providing technical support to private consumer shopping sites"], "The Primary User registers the department, manages user access rights, and ensures compliance with government purchasing guidelines."),
    ("On GeM, what are the distinct roles assigned to 'Secondary Users'?", "Buyer (creates bids and issues orders), Consignee (receives goods and issues CRAC), and Paying Authority (releases payments)", ["Director, Clerk, Janitor, and Driver", "Auditor, Tax Collector, Customs Officer, and Judge", "Seller, Reseller, Transporter, and Warehouser"], "Segregation of duties between Buyer, Consignee, and Paying Authority prevents collusion and ensures internal audit checks."),
    ("What is 'Life Cycle Costing' (LCC) in public procurement evaluation?", "Evaluating the total cost of ownership including acquisition price, installation, operating costs, maintenance, and disposal", ["Ranking bids solely on the cheapest initial purchase price tag", "Measuring how long the vendor company has been in commercial business", "Calculating the average lifespan of company board directors"], "LCC prevents purchasing low-cost equipment that imposes catastrophic recurring electricity, fuel, or maintenance repair costs."),
    ("What is 'Quality and Cost Based Selection' (QCBS) used for in procurement?", "Procurement of specialized consultancy or professional services where technical quality and price are weighted (e.g., 80:20 or 70:30)", ["Procurement of standard mass-market bulk wheat and rice", "Purchasing standard office stationery like pens and paperclips", "Auctioning expired government motor vehicles"], "QCBS is applied to intellectual services where quality of methodology and personnel is paramount over pure lowest fee."),
    ("Under GFR Rule 144(xi), what restriction is imposed on procurement from countries sharing a land border with India?", "Bidders must be registered with the competent authority (DPIIT) and obtain political and security clearance from MEA and MHA", ["They are banned from visiting Indian tourist destinations", "They must pay an import tariff of 200% on all goods", "They can participate freely without any registration"], "Instituted in 2020 for national defense and cyber security, this rule screens bidders from adjacent land-border nations."),
    ("What is 'Staggered Delivery' in supply contract management?", "Supplying ordered quantities in scheduled periodic tranches over time rather than a single lump-sum shipment", ["Delivering goods only when delivery trucks are completely full", "Delaying delivery past the contractual deadline", "Shipping goods to five different international seaports"], "Staggered delivery matches supplier shipments to buyer consumption patterns, minimizing warehouse holding costs."),
    ("What is 'Deemed Acceptance' (Auto-CRAC) on the GeM portal?", "If a consignee does not approve or reject goods within 10 days of delivery, the system auto-generates CRAC to trigger payment", ["The automatic approval of tenders without opening financial bids", "The automatic registration of any private company as an OEM", "The automatic refund of all customer payments by the bank"], "Auto-CRAC protects sellers from administrative harassment, bureaucratic bottlenecks, and deliberate payment delays."),
    ("In procurement tenders, what is 'Corrigendum'?", "A formal published amendment or correction modifying the terms, specifications, or deadlines of a tender notice", ["The final legal termination of a contract for default", "The receipt issued for physical delivery of office goods", "A cash refund given to unsuccessful bidding participants"], "Corrigenda maintain public transparency whenever specifications or deadlines change prior to bid submission opening."),
    ("What is 'e-Challan' on the GeM portal during logistics fulfillment?", "A digital dispatch document generated by the seller indicating invoice details, batch numbers, and shipment quantities", ["A traffic police fine issued to delivery drivers for speeding", "An import license granted by the customs revenue department", "A certificate of corporate income tax exemption"], "The e-challan accompanies physical deliveries, allowing consignees to verify itemized packages against the digital purchase order."),
    ("What is 'Inspection Authority' in large-scale government procurement?", "An independent agency (such as RITES, DGS&D, or third-party labs) mandated to inspect goods before dispatch or at site", ["The local municipal health inspection officer", "The marketing director of the competing bidder", "The security guard stationed at the factory entrance gate"], "Pre-dispatch inspection ensures complex engineered equipment conforms to rigorous Indian Standards (BIS) before transport."),
    ("What is the 'Sub-contracting' restriction typically enforced under MSE procurement policies?", "MSE bidders claiming purchase preference cannot sub-contract more than 25% of the total contract value to non-MSE firms", ["MSE bidders can sub-contract 100% of the work to foreign firms", "MSEs are completely forbidden from hiring any employees", "Sub-contracting is permitted only to state government departments"], "This restriction prevents large corporations from using front MSE enterprises as shells to game public purchase preferences."),
    ("What is the primary role of the Central Public Procurement Portal (CPPP) in India?", "A centralized national portal hosting e-tenders across all central government ministries, departments, and CPSEs", ["A portal selling discount consumer goods to the general public", "A database tracking private stock market equity dividends", "A website for booking domestic train and flight passenger tickets"], "CPPP (eprocure.gov.in) provides a transparent single point of access to all advertised public e-procurement opportunities.")
]

