    ("In a QCBS tender with 70:30 technical-financial weighting, if Bidder A scores 90 technical marks and quotes Rs 100, while lowest Bidder B quotes Rs 80 with 75 technical marks, how is composite score calculated?", "Composite Score = (Technical Score * 0.70) + [(Lowest Price / Bidder Price) * 100 * 0.30]", ["Composite Score = (Technical Score * 0.30) + (Bidder Price * 0.70)", "Composite Score = (Technical Score + Bidder Price) / 2", "Composite Score = Technical Score - Bidder Price"], "Financial score is normalized against lowest quote: Sf = (F_min / F) * 100. Combined Score = 0.70 * St + 0.30 * Sf."),
    ("In the evaluation of life cycle costs for heavy capital equipment, what does 'Terminal Salvage Value' represent?", "The estimated net residual cash flow realized from selling or scrapping the asset at the end of its operational useful life", ["The total repair cost paid during the initial warranty year", "The penalty paid to contractors for terminating work early", "The customs duty levied on foreign replacement components"], "Salvage value is discounted back to present value and subtracted from total lifecycle ownership costs in capital appraisals."),
