    ("What does 'Bid Rigging' under Section 3(3)(d) of the Competition Act, 2002 specifically encompass?", "Cover bidding, bid suppression, bid rotation, and market allocation agreements that distort competitive bidding", ["Offering seasonal discounts to individual walk-in retail shoppers", "Submitting bids electronically through secured government portals", "Purchasing tender application documents from public counters"], "Bid rigging encompasses covert collusive schemes designed to predetermine the winning contractor and artificial prices."),
    ("What is 'Cover Bidding' (Complementary Bidding) in procurement fraud?", "Conspiring firms submit token bids deliberately priced too high or containing defects to ensure a pre-selected colluder wins", ["Purchasing insurance policies to cover physical transit damages", "Wrapping paper bid envelopes in plastic protective covers", "Bidding on behalf of a public sector welfare charity"], "Cover bidding creates the illusion of genuine competitive tendering while guaranteeing the chosen co-conspirator secures the contract."),
